      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5acad9ecc9dba010c9c3ec68|full_name}: I'm rephrasing a comment I removed earlier. \nLaunching the game in 3PT will then correctly identify if the user switches to 4/6PT. You say its not \"officially supported\" to then go back to 3PT but the game has at the very least now switched correctly to FBT even though you say its not officially supported to change without restarting the game. However, it fails to completely return the UI to the officially supported session that was launched in 3PT.\n\nI would say somewhere along here is still a bug where the game at least correctly switched from 3PT to 4/6PT, but then never gives the seated/standing toggle back if it reverts from the FBT to 3PT. Either someone is unofficially supporting not needing to restart the game to go from 3PT to FBT, or now more likely it would be great to see the UI return when going from FBT to 3PT as expected that the UI already changes when it detects FBT. It would be great to see both officially supported rather than one way working and the other not.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
    {
      "__v": 0,
      "_id": "5d7e13080a6bc57fbe3eaec2",
